  "notes": [
    "Live REA stdio MCP over the main+DllBattle carrier (session outputs/rea-battle-7, analyses and byte reads); every instruction and literal word equals the original DllBattle.cro bytes; no relocation is involved.",
    "Fourteen gem handlers have no Ghidra function (analyze_function refuses them); their listings come from ../battle_power/reproduction/decode_arm.py and equal the REA listing of the sibling named in same_shape_as (108a8ec0 or 108aa510) apart from the type constant and entry-relative addresses.",
    "1084c700 and 10881638 end in bx lr, which the decoder refuses; their listing is REA's.",
    "Static analysis plus host comparison; not a matching original build."
  ]
